# STATUS: BLOCKED on KEGG paer mapping (no network, no local KEGG data)

Executed (all reproducible):
1. RDS inspection + export (no R needed): scripts/rds_extract.py + scripts/export_tables.py
   -> data/derived/GluFevsGluFePlus_full.csv (5828 genes x DESeq2 cols, 0 NA)
   -> data/derived/SuccvsGluFePlus_full.csv  (5828 genes, 0 NA)
   -> data/derived/down_GluFevsGluFePlus.csv  (91 genes: log2FC<=-1.5 & padj<=0.05)
   -> data/derived/down_SuccvsGluFePlus.csv  (289 genes, same cutoff)
2. ORA pipeline (enrichKEGG replica: scipy hypergeom right-tail + BH): scripts/ora_kegg_paer.py
   Validated end-to-end on SYNTHETIC mapping (data/synthetic/, results in data/results_demo/):
   planted pathways DEMO01/DEMO02 recovered as the only significant common ones. NOT KEGG data.
3. KEGG fetcher ready: scripts/fetch_kegg_paer.py (rest.kegg.jp /link/paer/pathway + /list/pathway/paer).
   Network re-tested at execution time: DNS + TCP egress blocked; no KEGG/keyring/GMT snapshot on disk.

To obtain the final number (single step, requires network OR a mapping TSV):
  python3 scripts/fetch_kegg_paer.py && python3 scripts/ora_kegg_paer.py \
    --map data/kegg/paer_link_pathway.tsv --names data/kegg/paer_pathway_names.tsv \
    --full-csv data/derived/*_full.csv \
    --down-csv data/derived/down_GluFevsGluFePlus.csv data/derived/down_SuccvsGluFePlus.csv \
    --labels GluFevsGluFePlus SuccvsGluFePlus
(or point --map to any gene<TAB>paXXXXX file). Outputs per-condition tables (pathway,name,k,N,K,n,p,padj,geneID),
common-pathway intersection for both universe variants (dataset_mapped PRIMARY vs kegg_all) + sensitivity flag.

No KEGG pathway count is reported because the gene->pathway mapping was unobtainable in this environment.
